.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ifg-notifications 1  "ifg-notifications 0.9.0"
.SH NAME
ifg\-notifications \- List and manage your notifications
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBifg notifications\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List and manage your notifications
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ifg\-notifications\-list(1)
List notifications (default when no subcommand is given)
.TP
ifg\-notifications\-read(1)
Mark one notification (or all of them) as read
.TP
ifg\-notifications\-delete(1)
Delete one notification
.TP
ifg\-notifications\-count(1)
Print the unread count
.TP
ifg\-notifications\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.9.0
